secureshellgo (1.5.0~noble1) noble; urgency=medium

  * A major update; the full list is in CHANGELOG.md.
  * The remote editor edits code like an IDE: detected indentation, Tab and
    auto-indent, comment and line shortcuts, per-file undo, and saves that
    never change bytes nobody edited.
  * Mosh, built in, for a terminal that survives roaming and sleep.
  * Sign in with ssh-agent (security keys included) and OpenSSH
    certificates; per-host agent and X11 forwarding.
  * A terminal that never dies: dead links are noticed and reconnected,
    transfers resume, and tmux or screen can keep the shell on the server.
  * Find in the terminal, clickable links, session logs, cursor, bell, font
    and scrollback settings.
  * Commands on many servers at once; compress, extract, search, duplicate
    and change owner in the file browser.
  * Translated into Simplified Chinese, Japanese, Brazilian Portuguese,
    Spanish, Russian, German, Korean and French.
  * Security fixes and hardening throughout; see CHANGELOG.md.

 -- Dhiva Labs <dhivakar1010@gmail.com>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0530

secureshellgo (1.4.4~noble1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Ctrl+L opens a location bar in the file browser: type or paste a path
    and go straight there instead of tapping through folders. "~" expands, a
    relative path resolves against the folder on screen, and a path to a file
    opens it in the editor while leaving the browser among its siblings. A
    path that cannot be reached reports the server's own message and leaves
    the listing untouched. Chips for /etc and /var/log sit in the bar.
  * The remote editor takes the keyboard when a file opens, so select all,
    copy, paste, cut and undo work immediately rather than only after the
    text has been clicked. An Edit menu and a keyboard-shortcuts dialog make
    the same actions reachable without a keyboard at all.
  * Clicking the file browser in the side-by-side layout now gives it the
    keyboard, which the location bar needs; click the terminal to type there
    again.

 -- Dhiva Labs <dhivakar1010@gmail.com>  Fri, 07 Aug 2026 22:15:00 +0530

